    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: e0560e683fde64ac6b0ff4c91893cbd43b7718e9 -->\n**Maintainer-requested shallow verification (Windows): clean.** `cargo test -p xtask`: 23 passed. Clippy `-D warnings`: clean. Dry run `cargo xtask release --version 9.9.9 --no-tag --dry-run` against origin/main's `release.ps1 -Version 9.9.9 -NoTag -DryRun` on a scratch branch: both exit 0 and all 10 phase headings match. The one extra line is the release gate tier's dry-run summary, the documented change of running `gate release`. The wrapper `release.ps1 -NoTag -DryRun -SkipGate` exits 0 and prints the manual tag steps. Without `--no-tag` it refuses by name (main is branch-protected). Not exercised: a real bump, build, sign, zip or installer, and macOS, Linux and FreeBSD. The maintainer asked for this check and the merge.",
